<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Place Stanislas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1752">1752</a>–<a href="/years/1755">1755</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Place Royale (Nancy)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Place Stanislas is a large square in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nancy">Nancy</a>, laid out in 1752–1755 as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/place-des-vosges">Place Royale</a> by the architect <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emmanuel-here">Emmanuel Héré</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stanislaw-leszczynski">Stanisław Leszczyński</a>, duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>, with a statue of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xv">Louis XV</a> at its centre. It is framed by the town hall and other pavilions and by gilded iron gates by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-lamour">Jean Lamour</a>. Renamed after Stanisław in 1831, it has been a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> since 1983.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/place-stanislas.jpg" alt="Place Stanislas" width="320" height="188" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nicolas Cornet · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vue_de_nuit_de_la_Place_Stanislas_%C3%A0_Nancy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
